      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T20:53:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What we are doing is copying up the sepolicy calculated sid from the child dentry (realpath) referencing the backing filesystem (upper or lower), into the parent node (dentry).\n\nOnly a _silent_ policy denial (-EACCES) from the underlying filesystems, but without dentry-\u003einode-\u003ei_security-\u003esid returned and initialized, the avc message will always report the target context as unlabeled (tcontext\u003du:object_r:unlabeled:s0) making audit2allow completely useless since the actual security target check was for the child sid.\n\nEACCES is generated by the _silent_ avc check, but nothing gets printed until the policy gets the ultimate handler return from the parent node.\n\nFor other union filesystems (eg: sdcardfs) the target context is not from the child node, but is a mount context; so admittedly an unique issue with overlayfs.",
      "parentUuid": "00253bd2_1fb49e94",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 289,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 289,
